      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While \"equality of opportunity\" maintains traditional risk assessment integrity, it often treats current disparities as inevitable, which doesn't fulfill a forward-looking ESG mandate. You can counter this by arguing that modern risk modeling can integrate fairness constraints, effectively finding the most accurate model *within* an acceptable margin of fairness. Therefore, the goal isn't sacrificing accuracy, but *redefining* acceptable accuracy to include ethical and social performance metrics. This positions fairness not as a trade-off, but as a critical, modern dimension of sound risk management.",
      "source": "target",
